### Title of Recipe

Chicken Katsu Curry [cheatmode]

### Ingredients

440g crumbed pub chicken breast schnitzels
1 tbs olive oil
1 large carrot, peeled, thickly sliced
2 medium potatoes, peeled, diced into 1.5cm cubes
1 brown onion, coarsely chopped
1 clove garlic, crushed
92g S&B golden curry mild sauce mix
250g (1 cup) white rice

### Method

Preheat the oven at 180°C (160°C fan forced) for 5 minutes. Cook chicken for 25 minutes until cooked through.

Meanwhile, heat oil in a frying pan over medium heat. Add carrot, potato, onion and garlic, and saute for 5 minutes. Add 2 cups water. Bring to a boil, then cover with lid and simmer for until potato softens.

Remove from heat and crumble in curry mixture. Stir until nearly dissolved. Return to a low heat and cook for 2-3 minutes or until the sauce is smooth.

Cook rice according to your ricecooker instructions (or in a saucepan). Slice chicken into 1.5cm strips. Divide rice between serving bowls. Top with curry mixture and chicken.

### Tips

Some thinly sliced squash would go well as a garnish.

Reducing the quantity of vegetables would still make a good (and arguably more authentic) dish. Removing the potato entirely could work well. 

More garlic is always welcome in my house

